# KNOWN GAP — a trailing comment is claimed by the WRONG DELIMITED REGION when
# two regions end on the same source line.
#
# `emit_trailing_comment_after` asks one question: is this comment on the same
# SOURCE LINE as the previous emit's last real character? That test is blind to
# DELIMITER BOUNDARIES. When a call's generic-argument list and the call's own
# `)` end on the same line, the generic-arg region's per-element hook runs
# FIRST and takes the comment off the shared forward-only cursor — so a comment
# the author wrote about the CALL is re-emitted as a trailing comment on the
# last TYPE ARGUMENT.
#
# Handed to the comment-attachment track by the delimited-list chokepoint track,
# and MEASURED there: the claiming rework (a typed comment table, one claiming
# chokepoint, runs claimed with their heads) does NOT close it, because nothing
# in that rework changes the same-source-line test. The fix is a region-aware
# claim: the trailing hook needs to know which delimited region owns the
# position it is claiming from.
#
# It is IDEMPOTENT and it RE-PARSES, which is exactly why no live fixture may
# pin the current output (Core #8 — a wrong answer that survives a second pass
# is the kind that gets ratified by accident).
#
# INTENDED (asserted by the `#[ignore]`d
# `known_gap_fmt_cross_region_trailing_claim`): the call's own comment stays with
# the CALL, on the line that closes it, and the last type argument keeps no
# comment of its own.
#
# OBSERVED (both before and after the R42 comment-attachment work): the call's
# comment is re-emitted as a trailing comment on the last TYPE ARGUMENT, one
# line above the line that closes the call, and the closing line comes back
# bare.
#
# ⚠ NO LINE OF THIS HEADER MAY SPELL A CELL MARKER, or the closing-call text
# the assertion looks for. The test locates its cell by searching the formatted
# output for the marker and taking the FIRST line that matches, so a header
# mention is found first — and a header comment line can never contain the
# closing text, so the test would stay RED even after the gap is fixed. The two
# markers and the closing text are therefore described here, never quoted.

auto b = wrap[
    int,
    # SEN gb-interior
    String](6)  # SEN B

void main():
    print(1)
